#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119798 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d216cc0e-58a7-5fab-b5fe-60c7656338cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Missing Numbers in the Matrix L of an LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065289c8-6083-5e28-b439-a1028276aaca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238133} {:answer/id #uuid "7fd39f64-1b5d-59ce-b5cb-1efe13447b54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239168} {:answer/id #uuid "86131357-6807-5be2-a552-ca9ef6c81d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239221} {:answer/id #uuid "beb2c18e-71f0-53f7-a28d-8c0f9fd6c7f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239717} {:answer/id #uuid "e97f219b-f69f-5751-b878-44e2f527fc2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fd39f64-1b5d-59ce-b5cb-1efe13447b54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239168} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc6ec522-771c-540e-977a-1cfa7f59fb4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cdec77c1-9cb6-5276-b408-5048c1f761dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-105599" :question/problem "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ -8 & 10 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\boxed{} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ -8 & 10 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 12 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{32}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $2$nd row of $A$ multiplied by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 12 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{32}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{2},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}=-(6)=-6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241086 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119798 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d216cc0e-58a7-5fab-b5fe-60c7656338cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Missing Numbers in the Matrix L of an LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a48f9b7-a09f-5e59-8fbc-b60875dc0064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238427} {:answer/id #uuid "7e07e1ff-90d7-55c6-8187-bec87865fc6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239150} {:answer/id #uuid "9142a26c-af0c-5413-a0a8-72e45c9c7f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239313} {:answer/id #uuid "a96a25da-05e1-5db0-812c-8666e834a401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239540} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc2a1b3-578b-5f36-8343-25768d288491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9142a26c-af0c-5413-a0a8-72e45c9c7f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239313} :answer-field/id #uuid "1474ec70-d403-5756-bc8f-af2e58baecae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca032623-0a65-5d05-a582-2e903aa5c322" :question/math-academy-id "q-105601" :question/problem "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\boxed{} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -18 & 17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{32}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $2$nd row of $A$ multiplied by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -18 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{32}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{2},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}=-(2)=-2.\n$$"}]}
